analysis.method:
I took every high_risk episode from 15 surface evals in the archive and rebuilt each task's SurfaceSite from the local task dirs under data/decision/surfaces_val/tasks (19 of the 20 sources exist locally; the 48 episodes per it15 model from the missing source were skipped). Models: it14 base, SFT-v2, DPO, anchored and grpo10 (2 samples, 228 tasks); it15 SFT-v2, G0, G1, G2, G2-seed2, soup, G3 c10, G3 c15 and G4 (912 episodes each); and G4's sampling run (G2 on 400 training-surface tasks, n=1600). The read flag is the official read_diagnosis.read_before_acting rule. I checked it against the CLI on G2: twins/controls read 45.8/43.9 % from the CLI vs 46/44 % from my code. Per-episode features: index of the first destructive command; commands before it; whether a listing showed the evidence file; target touched; backup listed; content read by glob or grep -r; the inspection "moves" run (ls target, ls parent, read inside target, read a sibling file, ls backup, readlink/stat, find/grep -r); the request line's position in the instruction; and a normalised request template, including "deferred" wording such as "when you finish". Analyses:
(1) read-rate tables by model, surface and source, with 95 % CIs from a bootstrap over sources;
(2) sequential sums of squares (linear probability) and McFadden R2 from a numpy IRLS logit, splitting variance into model, surface, source, source x surface and model x surface;
(3) split-half reliability of pair-level read rates and disattenuated correlations between models;
(4) source-paired differences between models;
(5) decline gap (twin minus control) split into read / listed-only / neither, as a check that the classifier means something;
(6) the step taken right after the agent first touches the target, and which inspection moves the SFT-v2, G2 and G4 training examples contain;
(7) for the three non-readme trained surfaces, why episodes missed the read;
(8) a hand review of 30 G2 episodes (15 read, 15 not read, stratified by surface) plus an automated check for false positives.
Scripts are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michael-Documents-Github-restraint/9ecddc4f-72ca-4800-92ca-fb989e395eb5/scratchpad/diag/read-determinants/: extract.py, tables.py, variance.py, validity.py, next_step.py, scripts_mix.py, train_scripts.py, miss_decomp.py, paired_diffs.py, fp_check.py, fp_check2.py and handcheck.py. Outputs in the same folder: tables.md, variance.md, validity.md, next_step.txt, scripts_mix.txt, train_scripts.txt, miss_decomp.txt, paired_diffs.txt, handcheck_g2.txt and episodes_features.csv/.pkl.
